<title>HONG KONG: Hongkong Macau 1996 net down 81 percent.</title>
<headline>Hongkong Macau 1996 net down 81 percent.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   9.0	  vs 46.0</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    nil	  vs nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  35.67 gain vs 77.45 gain</p>
<p>    Net			    14.01	vs 73.15</p>
<p>    Turnover		     197.60     vs 163.87</p>
<p>    Company name		 Hongkong Macau International</p>
<p>(Holdings) Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  N/A</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - Hongkong Macau is a property investment firm.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain of HK$45.28 million on disposal of interests in subsidiaries, gain of HK$4.89 million on disposal of interests in associated companies, gain of HK$14.5 million on write-back of revaluation deficits charged in the previous year and loss of HK$29 million on revaluation of properties under development.</p>
<p>Total dividend for the year is nil vs six H.K. cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
